'''''Pityrogramma calomelanos''''',<ref>{{Cite web |title=silver fern (Pityrogramma calomelanos) |url=https://www.inaturalist.org/taxa/166944-Pityrogramma-calomelanos |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=iNaturalist |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Pityrogramma calomelanos / Species Page / Plant Atlas |url=https://florida.plantatlas.usf.edu/plant/species/1751 |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=florida.plantatlas.usf.edu}}</ref> commonly known as the silver fern,<ref>{{Cite web |title=NParks {{!}} Pityrogramma calomelanos |url=https://www.nparks.gov.sg/florafaunaweb/flora/1/5/1561 |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=www.nparks.gov.sg}}</ref> is a rhizomatous geophyte or lithophyte native to [[Mexico]] and Tropical America.<ref>{{Cite web |title=India Flora Online |url=https://indiaflora-ces.iisc.ac.in/herbsheet.php?id=277&cat=15 |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=indiaflora-ces.iisc.ac.in}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Pityrogramma calomelanos - Useful Tropical Plants |url=https://tropical.theferns.info/viewtropical.php?id=Pityrogramma+calomelanos |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=tropical.theferns.info}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Pityrogramma calomelanos (Silverback Fern) - FSUS |url=https://fsus.ncbg.unc.edu/main.php?pg=show-taxon.php&plantname=pityrogramma+calomelanos |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=fsus.ncbg.unc.edu |language=en}}</ref> It grows mainly in subtropical regions and has been introduced widely across [[Asia]], [[Africa]], and [[Pacific islands]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pityrogramma calomelanos (L.) Link {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:17345640-1 |access-date=2025-09-18 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

